  "notes": "Yamamoto-first discovery pass under the current durable repository authority. docs/PRIORITIES.md, docs/EDITORIAL.md, docs/DOMAINS.md, and radar/inbox/README.md were reread before research or grading. Fresh Tsuyoshi Yamamoto checks covered Jazz House ALFIE, BODY&SOUL, current schedule traces, Space M&A and credible Japanese-jazz sources. The Space M&A dates returned by the pass, including September 29, October 30, November 28 and December 28, are already represented in canonical/curated/processed intake, and no additional unrepresented Yamamoto appearance was verified. The broader corridor pass found two unrepresented National Sawdust performances that clear Stage 1 for event-specific reasons. Jeffrey Zeigler's We Were Fridays is the public world premiere and album-release engagement of a multi-year cello/electronics/dance work rooted in Gullah cultural memory and the Black diaspora, with new compositions by Tamar-kali, Etienne Charles, Hannah Ishizaki and Zeigler and choreography by Reggie Regg Roc Gray. Lara Somogyi's a [time] patterned is the New York premiere of a newly released harp-centered work built from extended harp technique, electronics, pedal textures, tape processes and field recordings. Stage 2 assigns A+ to We Were Fridays because the premiere engagement is actively worth making room for, but not S: National Sawdust presents a second matinee the next day and the producing organization explicitly says the work will tour nationally and internationally, so A+ captures the recommendation without manufacturing scarcity. Somogyi receives A: the New York premiere and instrumental design make the performance worth RADAR admission, while a multi-city album-release run and active project make attend-if-convenient the durable recommendation. John Zorn's Flatlands at National Sawdust was reviewed but not added: the same new trio project is already represented in RADAR by its September 5 Solar Myth performance, and the September 12 National Sawdust date did not establish a distinct performance-specific hook beyond another stop by the same touring project. Recent/current RADAR intake was rechecked as a sanity test and remains concentrated in A/A+ with S/S+ reserved for scarcity; this batch adds A 1 / A+ 1 / S 0 / S+ 0.",
